  <section class="abstract" aria-label="Abstract">
    <span class="abstract-label">Abstract</span>
    <p>
      I’m an engineer who would rather ship the code than stand at the bench
      all day, so the hardware stays within arm’s reach and I stay in the
      chair. I work at Nuro —
      self-driving cars, imagine Waymo,
      except we do the software stack and then make it talk to a bunch of
      automotive and platform partners. When autonomy falls short, we put
      the car back on the road. We call it waypointing, which is a cute
      name for <s>remote control</s> “please do not stay stuck in a parking
      lot.”
    </p>
    <p>
      Day to day that is cameras, live streaming, real-time comms, networks,
      simulation, making GPU clusters compatible and actually fast. A ton of
      stuff meshed together so a safety-critical system stays extremely
      reliable and low-latency when precision matters so, so much.
    </p>
  </section>
